IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc-definitions`
IMPORT `ccc13-logic`

-- ccc13-fraud.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, Part X (Fraudulent Transactions Relating to Contracts and Trade):
-- section 379 (goods), section 380 (fraud), section 380.1 (sentencing), section 380.2 (prohibition order), section 381 (using the mails to defraud).
-- Written by part agent ccc13 from a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW THE ANSWERS READ. An offence function answers JUST TRUE when every element the text lists is met; JUST FALSE when an element the text states as a
-- condition ("Every one who ...") is not met (read as the text's "if": marginal reading (a), NOTES.md fork F1); NOTHING when a borrowed term, taken from the keel's
-- `s 2 ...` functions, is itself NOTHING. A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. A punishment function answers the limbs the text states, one Punishment each.
-- Where the text says "punishable on summary conviction" and states no penalty, the limb is the section 787(1) answer, which another part computes: it is an input.

§ `Part X -- Fraudulent Transactions Relating to Contracts and Trade`

§§ `Section 379 -- Interpretation: goods`

-- goods means anything that is the subject of trade or commerce. "In this Part" scopes it to ss 379 to 447.1 of this part's range and beyond to Part X only.
-- src:7147 | Interpretation
-- src:7148 | Definition of goods
-- src:7149 | 379 In this Part, goods means anything that is the subject of trade or commerce.
@ref s 379 (src:7147-7149)
GIVEN `the thing is the subject of trade or commerce` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 379 goods` MEANS
    IF `the thing is the subject of trade or commerce`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "goods means anything that is the subject of trade or commerce"

§§ `Section 380 -- Fraud`

-- (1) Every one who, by deceit, falsehood or other fraudulent means, ... defrauds the public or any person ... of any property, money or valuable security or any service.
-- "whether or not it is a false pretence within the meaning of this Act" and "whether ascertained or not" widen nothing and are not inputs.
-- src:7151 | Fraud
-- src:7152 | Fraud
-- src:7153 | 380 (1) Every one who, by deceit, falsehood or other fraudulent means, whether or not it is a false pretence within the meaning of this Act, defrauds the public or any person, whether ascertained or not, of any property, money or valuable security or any service,
-- src:7154 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to a term of imprisonment not exceeding fourteen years, where the subject-matter of the offence is a testamentary instrument or the value of the subject-matter of the offence exceeds five thousand dollars; or
-- src:7155 | (b) is guilty
-- src:7156 | (i) of an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years, or
-- src:7157 | (ii) of an offence punishable on summary conviction,
-- src:7158 | where the value of the subject-matter of the offence does not exceed five thousand dollars.
@ref s 380(1) (src:7151-7158)
GIVEN `the person acts by deceit, falsehood or other fraudulent means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person defrauds the public or any person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what the person defrauds of, as property` IS A `s 2 property kind`
      `what the person defrauds of is money` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what the person defrauds of, as a valuable security` IS A `s 2 valuable security kind`
      `what the person defrauds of is a service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 380(1) the conduct is the offence of fraud` MEANS
    IF `the person acts by deceit, falsehood or other fraudulent means` AND `the person defrauds the public or any person`
    THEN `ccc13 any of` (LIST `s 2 property` `what the person defrauds of, as property`
                            , JUST `what the person defrauds of is money`
                            , `s 2 valuable security` `what the person defrauds of, as a valuable security`
                            , JUST `what the person defrauds of is a service`)
         -- JUST FALSE when the thing is none of property, money, valuable security or service: FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "of any property, money or valuable security or any service"; NOTHING passes through from s 2 property and s 2 valuable security (NOTHING-kind (includes))
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one who, by deceit, falsehood or other fraudulent means"

-- (a) ... where the subject-matter of the offence is a testamentary instrument or the value of the subject-matter of the offence exceeds five thousand dollars.
-- The testamentary instrument is the person's own judgment (the brief: an open-textured term is a plain input); s 2 "testamentary instrument" says "includes", so it is asked as MAYBE BOOLEAN.
@ref s 380(1)(a) (the limb applies) (src:7154-7154)
GIVEN `the subject-matter of the offence is a testamentary instrument, by s 2 testamentary instrument` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the value of the subject-matter of the offence, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 380(1)(a) the subject-matter is a testamentary instrument or its value exceeds five thousand dollars` MEANS
    `ccc13 any of` (LIST `the subject-matter of the offence is a testamentary instrument, by s 2 testamentary instrument`
                        , JUST (`the value of the subject-matter of the offence, in dollars` GREATER THAN 5000))
    -- JUST FALSE when neither: FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the subject-matter of the offence is a testamentary instrument or the value of the subject-matter of the offence exceeds five thousand dollars"

-- (b) ... where the value of the subject-matter of the offence does not exceed five thousand dollars.
@ref s 380(1)(b) (the limb applies) (src:7155-7158)
GIVEN `the value of the subject-matter of the offence, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 380(1)(b) the value of the subject-matter does not exceed five thousand dollars` MEANS
    IF `the value of the subject-matter of the offence, in dollars` AT MOST 5000
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the value of the subject-matter of the offence does not exceed five thousand dollars"

-- The limbs the text states. (a) indictable, not exceeding fourteen years; (b)(i) indictable, not exceeding two years; (b)(ii) summary conviction, no penalty stated: s 787(1).
@ref s 380(1)(a) (the limb) (src:7154-7154)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 380(1)(a) the limb` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref s 380(1)(b)(i) (the limb) (src:7156-7156)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 380(1)(b)(i) the limb` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- Fork F3: a testamentary instrument worth five thousand dollars or less is within (a) (it is a testamentary instrument) and within (b) (the value does not exceed).
-- The text gives two classes and two maxima for it: the answer is NOTHING, not a choice made for the text.
@ref s 380(1) (the punishments) (src:7153-7158)
GIVEN `the limb (a) applies, by s 380(1)(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the limb (b) applies, by s 380(1)(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF Punishment)
`s 380(1) the punishments` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the limb (a) applies, by s 380(1)(a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the limb (b) applies, by s 380(1)(b)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST (LIST `s 380(1)(a) the limb`)
        IF `the limb (a) applies, by s 380(1)(a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `the limb (b) applies, by s 380(1)(b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST (LIST `s 380(1)(b)(i) the limb`, `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): both limbs apply to a testamentary instrument of low value (fork F3), or a limb is itself NOTHING

@ref s 380(1) (the class of the offence) (src:7153-7158)
GIVEN `the limb (a) applies, by s 380(1)(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the limb (b) applies, by s 380(1)(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Class of offence`)
`s 380(1) the class of the offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the limb (a) applies, by s 380(1)(a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the limb (b) applies, by s 380(1)(b)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST `an indictable offence`
        IF `the limb (a) applies, by s 380(1)(a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `the limb (b) applies, by s 380(1)(b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): see fork F3

-- (1.1) When a person is prosecuted on indictment and convicted of one or more offences referred to in subsection (1), the court that imposes the sentence shall impose a
-- minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of two years if the total value of the subject-matter of the offences exceeds one million dollars.
-- src:7159 | Minimum punishment
-- src:7160 | (1.1) When a person is prosecuted on indictment and convicted of one or more offences referred to in subsection (1), the court that imposes the sentence shall impose a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of two years if the total value of the subject-matter of the offences exceeds one million dollars.
@ref s 380(1.1) (src:7159-7160)
GIVEN `the person is prosecuted on indictment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is convicted of one or more offences referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the total value of the subject-matter of the offences, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 380(1.1) the court shall impose a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of two years` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the person is prosecuted on indictment` AND `the person is convicted of one or more offences referred to in subsection (1)`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When a person is prosecuted on indictment and convicted of one or more offences referred to in subsection (1)"
    ELSE IF `the total value of the subject-matter of the offences, in dollars` GREATER THAN 1000000
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the total value of the subject-matter of the offences exceeds one million dollars"

-- The minimum the subsection imposes, as a Punishment limb (indictable, a minimum of two years; no maximum is stated here).
@ref s 380(1.1) (the minimum punishment) (src:7159-7160)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 380(1.1) the minimum punishment` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

DECLARE `s 380(1.1) act of the court` IS ONE OF
    `s 380(1.1) impose a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of two years`

-- The duty as a regulative rule: the court MUST impose it. The text gives no time limit and no consequence, so there is no WITHIN, no HENCE and no LEST.
@ref s 380(1.1) (the duty of the court) (src:7159-7160)
GIVEN `the court shall impose, by s 380(1.1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 380(1.1) act of the court`
`s 380(1.1) the duty of the court` MEANS
    IF `the court shall impose, by s 380(1.1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the court` MUST `s 380(1.1) impose a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of two years`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (2) Every one who, by deceit, falsehood or other fraudulent means, ..., with intent to defraud, affects the public market price of stocks, shares, merchandise or anything that is offered for sale to the public.
-- src:7161 | Affecting public market
-- src:7162 | (2) Every one who, by deceit, falsehood or other fraudulent means, whether or not it is a false pretence within the meaning of this Act, with intent to defraud, affects the public market price of stocks, shares, merchandise or anything that is offered for sale to the public is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years.
@ref s 380(2) (src:7161-7162)
GIVEN `the person acts by deceit, falsehood or other fraudulent means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts with intent to defraud` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person affects the public market price of stocks, shares, merchandise or anything that is offered for sale to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 380(2) the conduct is the offence of affecting the public market` MEANS
    IF `the person acts by deceit, falsehood or other fraudulent means` AND `the person acts with intent to defraud` AND `the person affects the public market price of stocks, shares, merchandise or anything that is offered for sale to the public`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one who, by deceit, falsehood or other fraudulent means"

@ref s 380(2) (the punishments) (src:7161-7162)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 380(2) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states

@ref s 380(2) (the class of the offence) (src:7161-7162)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 380(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

§§ `Section 380.1 -- Sentencing: aggravating circumstances and non-mitigating factors`

-- (1) Without limiting the generality of section 718.2, where a court imposes a sentence for an offence referred to in section 380, 382, 382.1 or 400, it shall consider
-- the following as aggravating circumstances: (a) ... (f). The offence is tested by section number (seam rule R1), not by an input from the part that owns it.
-- src:7163 | Sentencing — aggravating circumstances
-- src:7164 | 380.1 (1) Without limiting the generality of section 718.2, where a court imposes a sentence for an offence referred to in section 380, 382, 382.1 or 400, it shall consider the following as aggravating circumstances:
-- src:7165 | (a) the magnitude, complexity, duration or degree of planning of the fraud committed was significant;
-- src:7166 | (b) the offence adversely affected, or had the potential to adversely affect, the stability of the Canadian economy or financial system or any financial market in Canada or investor confidence in such a financial market;
-- src:7167 | (c) the offence involved a large number of victims;
-- src:7168 | (c.1) the offence had a significant impact on the victims given their personal circumstances including their age, health and financial situation;
-- src:7169 | (d) in committing the offence, the offender took advantage of the high regard in which the offender was held in the community;
-- src:7170 | (e) the offender did not comply with a licensing requirement, or professional standard, that is normally applicable to the activity or conduct that forms the subject-matter of the offence; and
-- src:7171 | (f) the offender concealed or destroyed records related to the fraud or to the disbursement of the proceeds of the fraud.
@ref s 380.1(1) (src:7163-7171)
DECLARE `s 380.1(1) circumstance` IS ONE OF
    `s 380.1(1) the magnitude, complexity, duration or degree of planning of the fraud committed was significant`   -- (a)
    `s 380.1(1) the offence adversely affected, or had the potential to adversely affect, the stability of the Canadian economy or financial system or any financial market in Canada or investor confidence in such a financial market`   -- (b)
    `s 380.1(1) the offence involved a large number of victims`   -- (c)
    `s 380.1(1) the offence had a significant impact on the victims given their personal circumstances including their age, health and financial situation`   -- (c.1)
    `s 380.1(1) in committing the offence, the offender took advantage of the high regard in which the offender was held in the community`   -- (d)
    `s 380.1(1) the offender did not comply with a licensing requirement, or professional standard, that is normally applicable to the activity or conduct that forms the subject-matter of the offence`   -- (e)
    `s 380.1(1) the offender concealed or destroyed records related to the fraud or to the disbursement of the proceeds of the fraud`   -- (f)
    `s 380.1(1) the circumstance is none of those in paragraphs (a) to (f)`

@ref s 380.1(1) (src:7163-7171)
GIVEN `the offence for which the sentence is imposed` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      circumstance IS A `s 380.1(1) circumstance`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 380.1(1) the court shall consider the circumstance as aggravating` MEANS
    IF NOT (   `the offence for which the sentence is imposed`'s section EQUALS 380
            OR `the offence for which the sentence is imposed`'s section EQUALS 382
            OR `the offence for which the sentence is imposed`'s section EQUALS 382.1
            OR `the offence for which the sentence is imposed`'s section EQUALS 400)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a court imposes a sentence for an offence referred to in section 380, 382, 382.1 or 400"
    ELSE CONSIDER circumstance
         WHEN `s 380.1(1) the circumstance is none of those in paragraphs (a) to (f)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraphs list the circumstances; a circumstance outside them is not one the paragraphs make aggravating
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 380.1 act of the court` IS ONE OF
    `s 380.1(1) consider the circumstance as an aggravating circumstance`
    `s 380.1(1.1) consider as an aggravating circumstance the fact that the value of the fraud committed exceeded one million dollars`
    `s 380.1(2) consider the circumstance as a mitigating circumstance`
    `s 380.1(3) cause the aggravating and mitigating circumstances it took into account to be stated in the record`

-- The duty: the court MUST consider the circumstance as aggravating. No time limit and no consequence are stated.
@ref s 380.1(1) (the duty of the court) (src:7163-7171)
GIVEN `the court shall consider, by s 380.1(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 380.1 act of the court`
`s 380.1(1) the duty of the court` MEANS
    IF `the court shall consider, by s 380.1(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the court` MUST `s 380.1(1) consider the circumstance as an aggravating circumstance`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (1.1) Without limiting the generality of section 718.2, when a court imposes a sentence for an offence referred to in section 382, 382.1 or 400, it shall also consider as an
-- aggravating circumstance the fact that the value of the fraud committed exceeded one million dollars. Section 380 is NOT in this list, and the value is tested at one million.
-- src:7172 | Aggravating circumstance — value of the fraud
-- src:7173 | (1.1) Without limiting the generality of section 718.2, when a court imposes a sentence for an offence referred to in section 382, 382.1 or 400, it shall also consider as an aggravating circumstance the fact that the value of the fraud committed exceeded one million dollars.
@ref s 380.1(1.1) (src:7172-7173)
GIVEN `the offence for which the sentence is imposed` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the value of the fraud committed, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 380.1(1.1) the court shall consider the value of the fraud as aggravating` MEANS
    IF NOT (   `the offence for which the sentence is imposed`'s section EQUALS 382
            OR `the offence for which the sentence is imposed`'s section EQUALS 382.1
            OR `the offence for which the sentence is imposed`'s section EQUALS 400)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when a court imposes a sentence for an offence referred to in section 382, 382.1 or 400"
    ELSE IF `the value of the fraud committed, in dollars` GREATER THAN 1000000
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is to consider the fact that the value exceeded one million dollars; where it did not exceed, the subsection is silent

@ref s 380.1(1.1) (the duty of the court) (src:7172-7173)
GIVEN `the court shall consider, by s 380.1(1.1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 380.1 act of the court`
`s 380.1(1.1) the duty of the court` MEANS
    IF `the court shall consider, by s 380.1(1.1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the court` MUST `s 380.1(1.1) consider as an aggravating circumstance the fact that the value of the fraud committed exceeded one million dollars`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (2) When a court imposes a sentence for an offence referred to in section 380, 382, 382.1 or 400, it shall not consider as mitigating circumstances the offender's employment,
-- employment skills or status or reputation in the community if those circumstances were relevant to, contributed to, or were used in the commission of the offence.
-- src:7174 | Non-mitigating factors
-- src:7175 | (2) When a court imposes a sentence for an offence referred to in section 380, 382, 382.1 or 400, it shall not consider as mitigating circumstances the offender’s employment, employment skills or status or reputation in the community if those circumstances were relevant to, contributed to, or were used in the commission of the offence.
@ref s 380.1(2) (src:7174-7175)
DECLARE `s 380.1(2) circumstance` IS ONE OF
    `s 380.1(2) the offender’s employment`
    `s 380.1(2) the offender’s employment skills`
    `s 380.1(2) the offender’s status or reputation in the community`
    `s 380.1(2) a circumstance that is none of those`

@ref s 380.1(2) (src:7174-7175)
GIVEN `the offence for which the sentence is imposed` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      circumstance IS A `s 380.1(2) circumstance`
      `the circumstance was relevant to, contributed to, or was used in the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 380.1(2) the court shall not consider the circumstance as mitigating` MEANS
    IF NOT (   `the offence for which the sentence is imposed`'s section EQUALS 380
            OR `the offence for which the sentence is imposed`'s section EQUALS 382
            OR `the offence for which the sentence is imposed`'s section EQUALS 382.1
            OR `the offence for which the sentence is imposed`'s section EQUALS 400)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When a court imposes a sentence for an offence referred to in section 380, 382, 382.1 or 400"
    ELSE IF circumstance EQUALS `s 380.1(2) a circumstance that is none of those`
         THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): only employment, employment skills and status or reputation are named
         ELSE IF `the circumstance was relevant to, contributed to, or was used in the commission of the offence`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if those circumstances were relevant to, contributed to, or were used in the commission of the offence"

-- A prohibition: SHANT. The act is "consider as mitigating", so the court respects the prohibition by not doing it.
@ref s 380.1(2) (the prohibition on the court) (src:7174-7175)
GIVEN `the court shall not consider, by s 380.1(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 380.1 act of the court`
`s 380.1(2) the prohibition on the court` MEANS
