§§ `Section 380.2 -- Prohibition order`

-- (1) When an offender is convicted, or is discharged on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under section 730, of an offence referred to in subsection 380(1), the court that
-- sentences or discharges the offender ... may make ... an order prohibiting the offender from seeking, obtaining or continuing any employment, or becoming or being a volunteer in any capacity,
-- that involves having authority over the real property, money or valuable security of another person.
-- src:7178 | Prohibition order
-- src:7179 | 380.2 (1) When an offender is convicted, or is discharged on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under section 730, of an offence referred to in subsection 380(1), the court that sentences or discharges the offender, in addition to any other punishment that may be imposed for that offence or any other condition prescribed in the order of discharge, may make, subject to the conditions or exemptions that the court directs, an order prohibiting the offender from seeking, obtaining or continuing any employment, or becoming or being a volunteer in any capacity, that involves having authority over the real property, money or valuable security of another person.
@ref s 380.2(1) (src:7178-7179)
GIVEN `the offender is convicted of an offence referred to in subsection 380(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender is discharged on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under section 730 of an offence referred to in subsection 380(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 380.2(1) the court may make an order prohibiting the offender from employment or volunteering` MEANS
    IF `the offender is convicted of an offence referred to in subsection 380(1)` OR `the offender is discharged on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under section 730 of an offence referred to in subsection 380(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When an offender is convicted, or is discharged on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under section 730"

DECLARE `s 380.2(1) activity` IS ONE OF
    `s 380.2(1) seeking, obtaining or continuing employment`
    `s 380.2(1) becoming or being a volunteer in any capacity`
    `s 380.2(1) an activity that is neither`

@ref s 380.2(1) (what the order may prohibit) (src:7178-7179)
GIVEN activity IS A `s 380.2(1) activity`
      `the employment or volunteer capacity involves having authority over the real property, money or valuable security of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 380.2(1) the activity is one the order may prohibit` MEANS
    IF activity EQUALS `s 380.2(1) an activity that is neither`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the order may prohibit seeking, obtaining or continuing employment, or becoming or being a volunteer
    ELSE IF `the employment or volunteer capacity involves having authority over the real property, money or valuable security of another person`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the order reaches only what "involves having authority over the real property, money or valuable security of another person"; the text has no "only" here

DECLARE `s 380.2 act of the court` IS ONE OF
    `s 380.2(1) make an order prohibiting the offender from employment or volunteering`
    `s 380.2(3) vary the conditions prescribed in the order`

-- A power of the court: MAY, with no LEST (a MAY with a LEST lapses differently on the two stable builds), so the permission has no consequence stated.
@ref s 380.2(1) (the power of the court) (src:7178-7179)
GIVEN `the court may make the order, by s 380.2(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 380.2 act of the court`
`s 380.2(1) the power of the court` MEANS
    IF `the court may make the order, by s 380.2(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the court` MAY `s 380.2(1) make an order prohibiting the offender from employment or volunteering`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (2) The prohibition may be for any period that the court considers appropriate, including any period to which the offender is sentenced to imprisonment.
-- src:7180 | Duration
-- src:7181 | (2) The prohibition may be for any period that the court considers appropriate, including any period to which the offender is sentenced to imprisonment.
@ref s 380.2(2) (src:7180-7181)
GIVEN `the court considers the period appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period is a period to which the offender is sentenced to imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 380.2(2) the prohibition may be for the period` MEANS
    IF `the court considers the period appropriate` OR `the period is a period to which the offender is sentenced to imprisonment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any period that the court considers appropriate"; a period the court does not consider appropriate is outside the grant

-- (3) A court that makes an order of prohibition or, if the court is for any reason unable to act, another court of equivalent jurisdiction in the same province, may, on application of the
-- offender or the prosecutor, require the offender to appear before it at any time and, after hearing the parties, that court may vary the conditions prescribed in the order if, in the opinion of the court,
-- the variation is desirable because of changed circumstances. The "if" is a gate on a power named "may": NOTHING when it fails (ruling of 2026-11-12, limit (1)), see fork F5.
-- src:7182 | Court may vary order
-- src:7183 | (3) A court that makes an order of prohibition or, if the court is for any reason unable to act, another court of equivalent jurisdiction in the same province, may, on application of the offender or the prosecutor, require the offender to appear before it at any time and, after hearing the parties, that court may vary the conditions prescribed in the order if, in the opinion of the court, the variation is desirable because of changed circumstances.
@ref s 380.2(3) (src:7182-7183)
GIVEN `the court is the court that made the order, or, if that court is for any reason unable to act, another court of equivalent jurisdiction in the same province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender or the prosecutor has applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has heard the parties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the opinion of the court the variation is desirable because of changed circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 380.2(3) the court may vary the conditions prescribed in the order` MEANS
    IF    `the court is the court that made the order, or, if that court is for any reason unable to act, another court of equivalent jurisdiction in the same province`
      AND `the offender or the prosecutor has applied`
      AND `the court has heard the parties`
      AND `in the opinion of the court the variation is desirable because of changed circumstances`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is given to that court, on application, after hearing the parties, "if, in the opinion of the court, the variation is desirable"

@ref s 380.2(3) (the power of the court) (src:7182-7183)
GIVEN `the court may vary the conditions, by s 380.2(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 380.2 act of the court`
`s 380.2(3) the power of the court` MEANS
    IF `the court may vary the conditions, by s 380.2(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the court` MAY `s 380.2(3) vary the conditions prescribed in the order`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (4) Every person who is bound by an order of prohibition and who does not comply with the order is guilty of (a) an indictable offence ... two years; or (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
-- src:7184 | Offence
-- src:7185 | (4) Every person who is bound by an order of prohibition and who does not comply with the order is guilty of
-- src:7186 | (a) an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years; or
-- src:7187 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 380.2(4) (src:7184-7187)
GIVEN `the person is bound by an order of prohibition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does not comply with the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 380.2(4) the conduct is the offence of not complying with an order of prohibition` MEANS
    IF `the person is bound by an order of prohibition` AND `the person does not comply with the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who is bound by an order of prohibition and who does not comply with the order"

@ref s 380.2(4) (the punishments) (src:7184-7187)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 380.2(4) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states
    , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb 2: the text states no penalty: s 787(1)

@ref s 380.2(4) (the class of the offence) (src:7184-7187)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 380.2(4) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

