§§ `Section 381 -- Using mails to defraud`

-- 381 Every person who makes use of the mails for the purpose of transmitting or delivering letters or circulars concerning schemes devised or intended to deceive or defraud the public,
-- or for the purpose of obtaining money under false pretences, is guilty of (a) an indictable offence ... two years; or (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
-- src:7190 | Using mails to defraud
-- src:7191 | 381 Every person who makes use of the mails for the purpose of transmitting or delivering letters or circulars concerning schemes devised or intended to deceive or defraud the public, or for the purpose of obtaining money under false pretences, is guilty of
-- src:7192 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or
-- src:7193 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 381 (src:7190-7193)
GIVEN `the person makes use of the mails` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is transmitting or delivering letters or circulars concerning schemes devised or intended to deceive or defraud the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is obtaining money under false pretences` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 381 the conduct is the offence of using the mails to defraud` MEANS
    IF `the person makes use of the mails` AND (   `the purpose is transmitting or delivering letters or circulars concerning schemes devised or intended to deceive or defraud the public`
                                              OR `the purpose is obtaining money under false pretences`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who makes use of the mails for the purpose of"

@ref s 381 (the punishments) (src:7190-7193)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 381 the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states
    , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb 2: the text states no penalty: s 787(1)

@ref s 381 (the class of the offence) (src:7190-7193)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 381 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
